WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions of "Empathia in our modern world" (MODERN, 2:00). The cues are the captions burned into the master (sha256 b0821063551b…),
read from its frames on 2026-11-27 (sampled four times a second) and checked by eye against the picture; on-screen interface text,
the title card and the end card are not captioned. Timings are to the nearest quarter second.

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.000
Our buildings are filled with remarkable technology.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.250
Yet understanding them,

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.250
and finding our way through them,

4
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.500
is still harder than it should be.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Meet Daniel. Forty minutes,

6
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.750
a terminal he's never seen.

7
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.500
Watch what happens when the building meets him halfway.

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.750
One scan, and the terminal explains itself.

9
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.250
His gate. His route. Step-free,

10
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.250
if he needs it.

11
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.500
Across the terminal,

12
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.750
Priya sees the same building through her role:

13
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.500
signage, systems and service,

14
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.250
all in context.

15
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.000
He sees his journey.

16
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.250
She sees her responsibility.

17
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.750
Same platform, different world.

18
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.500
Leah needs Room 214,

19
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.000
and her teacher needs that room ready to teach.

20
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.500
Leah finds her class.

21
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.250
Her teacher asks the room what it can do,

22
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.250
and Empathia Learn shows her, step by step.

23
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.250
For Marcus, the engineer,

24
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.500
the same room reveals what's behind the walls:

25
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.500
every device, every connection,

26
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.250
how it was commissioned.

27
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.750
The room never changed. The experience did.

28
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.250
Some places matter more.

29
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.250
A hospital should never feel like a maze,

30
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.500
least of all on the hardest day.

31
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.500
Elena scans the sign at the entrance.

32
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.000
Corridors, elevators, the way to the ward.

33
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.250
Directions only. Nothing private.

34
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.750
Behind the scenes,

35
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:30.250
staff and engineers each see what their role allows:

36
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.250
the systems, the dependencies, the evidence.

37
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.750
So the people who matter can simply be together.

38
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.500
Beneath it all, one foundation.

39
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.250
Places and people. Permissions.

40
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.750
Rooms and equipment. Search, intelligence,

41
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.500
evidence and learning.

42
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:52.000
Different places. Different people.

43
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.250
One connected world.

44
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Technology that understands its environment,

45
00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.750
and the people within it.
